{title: Did You Think to Pray?}
{artist: Mary Kidder & William Perkins}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[F]Ere you left your [Bb]room this [F]morning, ere you met the [C]busy day,
[F]did you sue for [Bb]loving [F]favor as a [C]shield to[F]day?

Chorus
O [F]how praying [Bb]rests the [F]weary! Prayer will change the [C]night to day;
[F]so when life seems [Bb]dark and [F]dreary, [C]don't forget to [F]pray.

Verse 2
[F]talove [C]Spirstay?
[F]dreapray.

Verse 3
[F]angrace, [C]noway?
[F]dreapray.

Verse 4
[F]on [C]bowed
[F]borday? [F]dreapray.
